course: dictionary
lesson: 3641
title: Fir
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fir is a tall evergreen tree. «Evergreen» means it keeps its green needles all year, even in winter. Its needles are flat, and its cones stand upright.
explain: Fir also means the wood of this tree. Context tells you which meaning is right. In «a dark green belt of spruce, pine, fir and larch», fir sits in a list of tree names, so it must be a tree. Swap in tree and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Clue words help too. «Cone-shaped trees» tells you the trees have cones, and «snow slides off» tells you they can cope with winter. When you are unsure, read the words around the new word and ask: what would fit here?
fact: A fir is a conifer: it keeps its needles in winter and grows cones.
fact: «Fir» means a tall evergreen tree with flat needles and upright cones.
fact: Many firs are used as Christmas trees.
fact: «Fir» can also mean the wood of this tree, which is used for building.
fact: «The taiga» is mostly spruce, pine, fir and larch, and it is the biggest land habitat on Earth.
exercise: «The taiga, or boreal forest, is mostly spruce, pine, fir and larch.» What is a fir? | A kind of cloud | A kind of animal | A kind of river | *A kind of tree
exercise: Many families buy a fir at Christmas. What is it most often used for? | A school desk | A bridge | A boat | *A Christmas tree
exercise: In «a dark green belt of spruce, pine, fir and larch», what kind of word is fir? | A colour | A place | *A tree name | A number
test: What does «evergreen» mean for a fir? | *It keeps its green needles all year | It is always red | It can only grow in water | It loses all its leaves in autumn
test: What does «upright cones» describe? | Cones that lie flat on the ground | Cones that are found only in the sea | *Cones that stand straight up | Cones that are made of metal
exam: Which tree has flat needles and upright cones, and is often a Christmas tree? | Oak | *Fir | Palm | Willow
